{
	"nodes": [
		{
			"id": "header",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## Neurochemistry\n\nDomain hub: transmitter life cycles, receptor families, the major signalling systems and modulatory control of circuit state.\n\n[[Neurochemistry Map|Open the domain map]] - snapshot of 2026-09-25; the map's *In this folder* section is the live view.",
			"x": 0,
			"y": 0,
			"width": 1680,
			"height": 170,
			"color": "#3F6FE0"
		},
		{
			"id": "g0",
			"type": "group",
			"label": "Structures",
			"x": 0,
			"y": 310,
			"width": 420,
			"height": 782
		},
		{
			"id": "s0",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Neurochemistry - Structures|Structures index]]**",
			"x": 30,
			"y": 360,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 88,
			"color": "#B8A4FF"
		},
		{
			"id": "t0_0",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Receptor families and second messengers]]**\n*structure* - 8 sources\n\nIonotropic versus metabotropic receptors, second-messenger cascades, and why receptor identity determines the effect of a transmitter.",
			"x": 30,
			"y": 508,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 242,
			"color": "#3F6FE0"
		},
		{
			"id": "t0_1",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Transmitter synthesis, release and clearance]]**\n*process* - 11 sources\n\nThe full life cycle of a neurotransmitter: synthesis from precursors, vesicular packaging, calcium-triggered release, and removal by transporters or enzymes.",
			"x": 30,
			"y": 810,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 242,
			"color": "#3F6FE0"
		},
		{
			"id": "g1",
			"type": "group",
			"label": "Mechanisms",
			"x": 420,
			"y": 310,
			"width": 420,
			"height": 3236
		},
		{
			"id": "s1",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Neurochemistry - Mechanisms|Mechanisms index]]**",
			"x": 450,
			"y": 360,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 88,
			"color": "#B8A4FF"
		},
		{
			"id": "t1_0",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Acetylcholine signalling]]**\n*mechanism* - 4 sources\n\nAcetylcholine pathways, nicotinic and muscarinic receptor families, enzymatic clearance, and the clinical associations that are often over-generalised.",
			"x": 450,
			"y": 508,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 218,
			"color": "#3F6FE0"
		},
		{
			"id": "t1_1",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Adenosine signalling]]**\n*mechanism* - 7 sources\n\nAdenosine as a metabolic signal and modulator of excitability, its receptors, and its relationship to caffeine and sleep pressure.",
			"x": 450,
			"y": 786,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 218,
			"color": "#3F6FE0"
		},
		{
			"id": "t1_2",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Dopamine signalling]]**\n*mechanism* - 8 sources\n\nDopamine pathways and receptor families, reward prediction error evidence, and the reasons a single 'reward molecule' story fails.",
			"x": 450,
			"y": 1064,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 218,
			"color": "#3F6FE0"
		},
		{
			"id": "t1_3",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Endocannabinoid signalling]]**\n*mechanism* - 1 sources\n\nOn-demand endocannabinoid synthesis, retrograde signalling at CB1 receptors, and how this differs from classical transmission.",
			"x": 450,
			"y": 1342,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 218,
			"color": "#3F6FE0"
		},
		{
			"id": "t1_4",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Glutamate and GABA]]**\n*mechanism* - 8 sources\n\nGlutamate and GABA as the fast excitatory and inhibitory channels, their metabolic coupling, spatial logic and receptor pharmacology.",
			"x": 450,
			"y": 1620,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 218,
			"color": "#3F6FE0"
		},
		{
			"id": "t1_5",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Histamine signalling]]**\n*mechanism* - 6 sources\n\nThe tuberomamillary histamine system, its four receptor types, and its role in wakefulness, attention and peripheral immune signalling.",
			"x": 450,
			"y": 1898,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 218,
			"color": "#3F6FE0"
		},
		{
			"id": "t1_6",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Monoamine reuptake and degradation]]**\n*process* - 10 sources\n\nHow dopamine, noradrenaline and serotonin are cleared from synapses, and why transporter and enzyme blockade have indirect and delayed effects.",
			"x": 450,
			"y": 2176,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 218,
			"color": "#3F6FE0"
		},
		{
			"id": "t1_7",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Neuromodulation and circuit state]]**\n*mechanism* - 6 sources\n\nHow modulators such as monoamines and acetylcholine change the properties of whole circuits, making the same anatomy produce different outputs.",
			"x": 450,
			"y": 2454,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 218,
			"color": "#3F6FE0"
		},
		{
			"id": "t1_8",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Neuropeptides and opioids]]**\n*structure* - 4 sources\n\nPeptide transmitters, their families and processing, and the opioid system as the best-characterised example of peptide signalling.",
			"x": 450,
			"y": 2732,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 218,
			"color": "#3F6FE0"
		},
		{
			"id": "t1_9",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Noradrenaline signalling]]**\n*mechanism* - 8 sources\n\nNoradrenaline sources, receptor families, inattentive and autonomic roles, and the inverted-U evidence from prefrontal circuits.",
			"x": 450,
			"y": 3010,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 218,
			"color": "#3F6FE0"
		},
		{
			"id": "t1_10",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Serotonin signalling]]**\n*mechanism* - 7 sources\n\nSerotonin distribution and receptor families, the treatment link, and why 'low serotonin' is not an adequate causal account.",
			"x": 450,
			"y": 3288,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 218,
			"color": "#3F6FE0"
		},
		{
			"id": "g2",
			"type": "group",
			"label": "Contested framing",
			"x": 840,
			"y": 310,
			"width": 420,
			"height": 734
		},
		{
			"id": "s2",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Neurochemistry - Contested framing|Contested framing index]]**",
			"x": 870,
			"y": 360,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 88,
			"color": "#B8A4FF"
		},
		{
			"id": "t2_0",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Chemical imbalance framing]]**\n*theory* - 6 sources\n\nWhy 'chemical imbalance' is a historical shorthand rather than a mechanism, what remains supportable, and the practical consequences of the difference.",
			"x": 870,
			"y": 508,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 218,
			"color": "#3F6FE0"
		},
		{
			"id": "t2_1",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Synaptic signalling model]]**\n*theory* - 8 sources\n\nThe stepwise synaptic signalling model, the evidence for each step, and the phenomena it omits such as volume transmission and neuromodulation.",
			"x": 870,
			"y": 786,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 218,
			"color": "#3F6FE0"
		},
		{
			"id": "g3",
			"type": "group",
			"label": "Most-cited evidence",
